1
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:28,069
It's nice to see you both here.
Two brothers together.

2
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:33,867
All right, well, Director Baek,
let me pour you a drink.

3
00:00:35,911 --> 00:00:38,412
I heard your little brother
was a standout,

4
00:00:38,413 --> 00:00:41,499
even way back during his tenure
at the Military Academy.

5
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:42,959
You must be very proud.

6
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:44,126
He's a work in progress.

7
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:46,837
You were kind to have him
at this important gathering.

8
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:48,256
Really, I'm grateful.

9
00:00:48,257 --> 00:00:50,299
Oh, come on. It's a casual get-together.

10
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:54,762
An opportunity to get a couple
of Academy alumni together and catch up.

11
00:00:54,763 --> 00:00:59,309
And I've been so impressed by what my men
have been able to accomplish lately.

12
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:03,437
I put this little thing together
to show my full appreciation.

13
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:08,777
Oh, by the way. I heard a rumor.
You two go way back, isn't that right?

14
00:01:09,653 --> 00:01:10,821
Oh, yes.

15
00:01:11,697 --> 00:01:14,073
At this point, I don't know
if it's fate or a curse,

16
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:16,993
but Director Baek
keeps following me around.

17
00:01:16,994 --> 00:01:20,622
You know, maybe we were tortured lovers
in another life or something.

18
00:01:23,709 --> 00:01:24,835
Right, who knows.

19
00:01:26,003 --> 00:01:28,046
You'd think we'd be sick of each other.

20
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:32,384
I guess some ties
can't be severed so easily.

21
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:35,887
You know what I mean, Advisor Jang?

22
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,599
You like me that much, huh?

23
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:42,269
Yes, you're all I think about.

24
00:01:46,356 --> 00:01:49,609
Eventually, even the thread
that holds us together will get cut.

25
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:53,030
Things happen in life
only when they're meant to.

26
00:01:53,822 --> 00:01:55,948
You can't impose your plans on it.

27
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:58,118
I'm amazed how little
you've changed, Baek.

28
00:01:59,536 --> 00:02:01,580
Still a gentleman on the surface,

29
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:05,042
but vicious underneath.

30
00:02:07,461 --> 00:02:10,588
Like some dog
acting like he doesn't bite, right?

31
00:02:15,385 --> 00:02:17,179
You haven't changed much either.

32
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:20,932
A few drinks and you're smashed,
aren't you?

33
00:02:21,975 --> 00:02:24,227
I can't hold my liquor, that's true.

34
00:02:25,228 --> 00:02:26,730
Here.

35
00:02:27,648 --> 00:02:29,483
Go ahead, let me pour you another.

36
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:32,319
Colonel Baek.

37
00:02:33,487 --> 00:02:34,779
I wish you would've told me

38
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:36,781
that your older brother
was going to show up.

39
00:02:41,787 --> 00:02:45,164
I suppose this was a mistake.
Clearly I'm not welcome here.

40
00:02:45,165 --> 00:02:48,209
All I wanted was to have a drink
on this important occasion.

41
00:02:48,210 --> 00:02:49,211
Well, then…

42
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:51,629
Can I speak to you?

43
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:52,631
Hey, now.

44
00:02:54,049 --> 00:02:55,883
Wait a minute, please.

45
00:02:55,884 --> 00:02:57,761
If you leave the table now…

46
00:02:59,054 --> 00:03:00,471
I'm gonna cry.

47
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:05,936
Hey, come on. Stay.

48
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:08,646
This alcohol isn't good enough.

49
00:03:08,647 --> 00:03:11,274
Colonel Ahn,
where's the most expensive bottle?

50
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:14,777
We can't serve Director Baek subpar booze.

51
00:03:14,778 --> 00:03:16,655
Sure thing, sir. I'll get the best bottle.

52
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:20,825
You like hard liquor, don't you?

53
00:03:20,826 --> 00:03:24,121
I have a feeling you drank plenty
when the President was around.

54
00:03:24,955 --> 00:03:26,289
Yeah, but…

55
00:03:26,915 --> 00:03:29,083
the price of the bottle
isn't what matters, right?

56
00:03:29,084 --> 00:03:30,960
It's more about who you're drinking with.

57
00:03:33,964 --> 00:03:36,633
Wow, spoken like a true gentleman, huh?

58
00:03:37,384 --> 00:03:38,510
You know something?

59
00:03:39,845 --> 00:03:42,555
Director Baek never gets drunk,
no matter how much he drinks.

60
00:03:42,556 --> 00:03:43,639
It's amazing.

61
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:46,308
Whoa, that's incredible.

62
00:03:46,309 --> 00:03:49,354
I guess someone's a pro
at holding his liquor, huh?

63
00:03:50,272 --> 00:03:51,898
Take your pick, Commander.

64
00:03:53,525 --> 00:03:55,901
Chivas!

65
00:04:01,283 --> 00:04:04,743
All right, Director Baek, let me
pour you a nice big glass of Chivas.

66
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:06,163
Ah, right.

67
00:04:11,001 --> 00:04:13,294
You too, Advisor Jang.

68
00:04:13,295 --> 00:04:14,962
Ah, sure.

69
00:04:22,846 --> 00:04:25,139
Would you like one, Colonel?

70
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:26,933
I would be grateful, sir.
Much appreciated.

71
00:04:28,894 --> 00:04:30,186
You should have one too.

72
00:04:30,187 --> 00:04:32,229
Oh, if you insist.

73
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:42,198
All right, now that we have someone
so distinguished at our table,

74
00:04:42,199 --> 00:04:44,826
I want to savor the moment.

75
00:04:45,911 --> 00:04:47,244
Everybody ready?

76
00:04:47,245 --> 00:04:48,537
-  Yes!
-  Let's do it!

77
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:49,748
All right, then.

78
00:04:52,584 --> 00:04:53,668
Great.

79
00:05:00,217 --> 00:05:02,927
Well, regardless
of whatever has happened

80
00:05:02,928 --> 00:05:04,678
between us up until now,

81
00:05:04,679 --> 00:05:06,972
starting today, we are united.

82
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:08,182
Am I right?

83
00:05:08,183 --> 00:05:10,393
-  Yes!
- Okay, then.

84
00:05:11,478 --> 00:05:12,561
We are!

85
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:14,022
We are one!

86
00:05:24,616 --> 00:05:27,910
Now that you've had a drink,
you should give us a song.

87
00:05:27,911 --> 00:05:29,120
Come on, bring in the band.

88
00:05:30,539 --> 00:05:32,499
Get the band. Come on, Nami.

89
00:05:33,083 --> 00:05:35,377
Wow, who knew you were such a partier.

90
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:48,556
♪ Through lofty mountains
And deep valleys ♪

91
00:05:48,557 --> 00:05:51,100
♪ Across the silent land ♪

92
00:05:52,978 --> 00:05:57,982
♪ We march to the snow-covered frontline ♪

93
00:05:57,983 --> 00:06:00,026
Colonel, hold on. Just stop.

94
00:06:00,694 --> 00:06:01,987
Just a minute.

95
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:05,990
Don't spoil the lively mood
with some old army song.

96
00:06:05,991 --> 00:06:07,700
Know anything else?

97
00:06:07,701 --> 00:06:09,952
I only know military tunes, sir.
Sorry about that.

98
00:06:09,953 --> 00:06:12,414
Ugh, no.

99
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:15,082
All right, forget it. Give me the mic.

100
00:06:17,961 --> 00:06:21,380
Man, right when I came off
my tour of Southeast Asia.

101
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:25,050
All right, all right.
The commander's taking the mic!

102
00:06:31,182 --> 00:06:32,808
One, two, three, and!

103
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:35,603
♪ That dark-eyed girl ♪

104
00:06:35,604 --> 00:06:36,687
Girl!

105
00:06:36,688 --> 00:06:39,189
♪ She may seem a little proud at first ♪

106
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:40,274
At first!

107
00:06:40,275 --> 00:06:43,319
♪ But her heart is as soft as silk ♪

108
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:45,947
♪ And I've truly fallen for her ♪

109
00:06:46,698 --> 00:06:49,074
♪ A beautiful heart is what makes
A woman beautiful ♪

110
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:50,159
Beautiful!

111
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:58,293
♪ A pretty face alone
Doesn't make a woman ♪

112
00:06:59,461 --> 00:07:00,711
♪ A woman who stays true
Once she give her heart ♪

113
00:07:00,712 --> 00:07:04,089
Now, if you cut
this red wire, the countdown will stop.

114
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:05,507
It has to be the red wire.

115
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:08,385
If you cut the blue one by mistake,
it'll go off immediately.

116
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:13,182
♪ A woman who
Stays true once she gives her heart ♪

117
00:07:13,183 --> 00:07:15,768
♪ That's what a real woman is ♪

118
00:07:15,769 --> 00:07:16,852
Sing it!

119
00:07:16,853 --> 00:07:23,484
♪ They say love can…
Make you blind ♪

120
00:07:23,485 --> 00:07:25,027
♪ But her… ♪

121
00:07:30,992 --> 00:07:33,953
A single mistake
could bring everything to an end.

122
00:07:35,747 --> 00:07:38,415
That's why you have to
put your life on the line,

123
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:40,626
because every move could be your last.

124
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,593
The truth is,
it might only be sheer luck

125
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:51,346
that you've survived as long as you have.

126
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:54,264
Then again…

127
00:07:54,265 --> 00:07:55,475
…maybe it's fate.

128
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:58,644
All right, let's keep it going!

129
00:07:58,645 --> 00:08:01,106
Colonel Ahn, you're up next!

130
00:08:02,649 --> 00:08:04,483
It's my honor, sir!

131
00:08:20,125 --> 00:08:21,458
So, how did it go?

132
00:08:39,018 --> 00:08:40,729
Motherfucker.

133
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:07,422
Everyone out.

134
00:09:08,423 --> 00:09:10,467
Hey, get out. Come on, out!

135
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:28,025
Shit, shit.

136
00:09:44,876 --> 00:09:45,919
Director.

137
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:49,798
The bomb's gone missing.

138
00:09:52,217 --> 00:09:53,551
It wasn't there.

139
00:09:55,011 --> 00:09:56,262
I don't know what happened.

140
00:09:58,223 --> 00:10:00,308
What do you mean it's gone,
you idiot?

141
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:05,874
Could Pyo have taken it?

142
00:11:06,374 --> 00:11:09,751
I've been keeping tabs on him, sir,
and there's been no contact with Jang.

143
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:11,045
It's a slim possibility.

144
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:15,175
Do you think your brother could've…

145
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:19,679
Sir, your brother could've taken it.

146
00:11:22,682 --> 00:11:25,018
Did he seem like
he knew something yesterday?

147
00:11:26,853 --> 00:11:29,230
If Jang had it, he'd be trying
to make moves on you already.

148
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:33,359
Maybe you should go talk to your brother.

149
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:42,159
I heard you were there, Colonel Baek.

150
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:43,285
Where?

151
00:11:43,286 --> 00:11:45,204
General Hwang's special meeting.

152
00:11:45,205 --> 00:11:46,289
So, how was it?

153
00:11:46,998 --> 00:11:49,334
Uneventful. He just thanked us
for our hard work.

154
00:11:50,168 --> 00:11:52,587
Still, it's a pretty
exclusive group, right?

155
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:56,841
A guy like me with no connections
wouldn't get invited in a million years.

156
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:00,178
I'll be quiet.

157
00:12:00,762 --> 00:12:02,012
Let's go.

158
00:12:11,606 --> 00:12:12,607
Morning, Chief.

159
00:12:13,858 --> 00:12:15,651
Oh, Baek. Who's this?

160
00:12:15,652 --> 00:12:18,446
He'll be assisting with
American military affairs from now on.

161
00:12:18,947 --> 00:12:20,781
Yes, sir! Captain Min Jonghwan.

162
00:12:20,782 --> 00:12:22,741
Well, Baek. You must be pretty busy.

163
00:12:22,742 --> 00:12:25,410
Look, the guy's smart.
Take him under your wing for me.

164
00:12:25,411 --> 00:12:26,996
Yeah, yeah, I got it.

165
00:12:27,956 --> 00:12:29,540
- Hey.
- Yes, sir.

166
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:32,835
Ever smoked American cigarettes?

167
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:34,629
Sorry?

168
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:38,716
They're hard to come by.
Just take one and be grateful.

169
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:42,719
- Take it.
- Yes, sir. Much appreciated.

170
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:44,806
- Baek, you want one or what?
- No, I'll pass.

171
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:46,599
Right.

172
00:12:47,225 --> 00:12:49,309
You probably have
plenty of rare commodities

173
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:50,937
stocked up at your brother's place.

174
00:13:01,281 --> 00:13:03,950
How's your sister? Feeling any better?

175
00:13:06,953 --> 00:13:08,997
I'm sorry, I heard she's in the hospital.

176
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:12,875
I'm asking because
I'm genuinely worried about her.

177
00:13:17,547 --> 00:13:18,548
Why?

178
00:13:19,257 --> 00:13:21,426
Don't wanna miss your chance
to interrogate her?

179
00:13:22,552 --> 00:13:23,720
No, that's not why…

180
00:13:27,849 --> 00:13:29,058
Okay, never mind.

181
00:13:30,268 --> 00:13:33,229
When she wakes up, just… let me know.

182
00:13:48,661 --> 00:13:49,996
About yesterday…

183
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:53,373
why do you think he showed up?

184
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:55,625
Because he was scared. You saw him.

185
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:57,502
He skulked up to the table
like a little mutt

186
00:13:57,503 --> 00:14:00,380
with his tail between his legs.

187
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:02,633
The man's an expert at backstabbing.

188
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:05,511
Can't trust a word out of his mouth.

189
00:14:09,766 --> 00:14:10,850
I guess you're right.

190
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:15,979
You know, at the KCIA, the first thing
they teach you there is how to lie.

191
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:19,941
Baek Kitae must be one slippery
little bastard, to say the least.

192
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:21,527
That slick piece of shit.

193
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:28,993
Okay, Jang.

194
00:14:30,495 --> 00:14:33,623
Here's where I'm at.
Just my opinion on our circumstances.

195
00:14:34,624 --> 00:14:39,795
Right now, the KCIA and the MSC
are basically performing the same job.

196
00:14:39,796 --> 00:14:41,589
Why do we need both of them?

197
00:14:42,381 --> 00:14:46,134
It's a complete waste,
for the government and the taxpayers.

198
00:14:46,135 --> 00:14:48,304
We gotta come up with a way
to fix that, don't we?

199
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:52,016
Say the word and I'm on it.

200
00:14:52,934 --> 00:14:54,227
I'll have Baek Kitae brought in.

201
00:14:56,104 --> 00:14:57,437
I've mentioned before

202
00:14:57,438 --> 00:15:00,357
that I won't bring the guy in
on meth charges.

203
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:26,634
What's his deal?

204
00:15:27,385 --> 00:15:29,136
DEPUTY DIRECTOR PYO HAKSU

205
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:40,940
What brings you here?

206
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:43,568
You're still running ops
to gather intel, right?

207
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:45,611
Of course.

208
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:48,489
I'm not gonna stop because of the JIH.

209
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:51,242
Without those, the KCIA's screwed.

210
00:16:00,835 --> 00:16:03,671
- And this is what you have on them?
- Yeah.

211
00:16:04,714 --> 00:16:06,632
We should know their people, shouldn't we?

212
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:09,635
You want to sit?

213
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:18,768
One thing I've learned is
Hwang Daesik really looks after his own.

214
00:16:18,769 --> 00:16:21,063
Anyone from his school or hometown,

215
00:16:21,856 --> 00:16:23,482
he holds them close. One big family.

216
00:16:25,526 --> 00:16:27,527
OFFICER PERSONNEL… RANK:
LIEUTENANT COLONEL / BAEK KIHYUN

217
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:29,237
I told my guys to investigate everybody.

218
00:16:29,238 --> 00:16:31,782
Some clueless idiot
threw Colonel Baek in there too.

219
00:16:33,117 --> 00:16:34,202
Don't worry about it.

220
00:16:35,036 --> 00:16:36,037
I'll take care of it.

221
00:16:43,961 --> 00:16:45,755
Send this to my office. All of it.

222
00:16:47,298 --> 00:16:48,382
Why?

223
00:16:50,176 --> 00:16:51,969
You never cared about this stuff.

224
00:16:54,722 --> 00:16:55,848
Do it.

225
00:17:01,896 --> 00:17:02,897
Very good.

226
00:17:11,906 --> 00:17:15,201
That bastard barks another damn order
at me, I swear I'm gonna…

227
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:20,915
Go ahead, come on back here,
you prick. That's right.

228
00:17:21,624 --> 00:17:24,210
You want me to send all the files,
you motherfucker?

229
00:17:25,127 --> 00:17:28,046
Shut your mouth, Baek,
you big, slimy piece of shit.

230
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:30,465
You can't just keep kicking me around.

231
00:17:30,466 --> 00:17:32,759
Yeah, move it, don't mess with me.

232
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,387
Shut your mouth, you bitch.

233
00:17:35,263 --> 00:17:37,682
I'm gonna take your chair. Check this out.

234
00:17:38,391 --> 00:17:39,642
How about that?

235
00:18:06,669 --> 00:18:08,004
Where the hell are you going?

236
00:18:09,005 --> 00:18:10,506
You didn't pick up the phone.

237
00:18:14,051 --> 00:18:15,677
Have something you wanna say?

238
00:18:15,678 --> 00:18:17,179
Yeah, why were you there?

239
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:23,102
Well, I might ask you the same question.

240
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:27,606
What exactly
were you trying to pull there,

241
00:18:27,607 --> 00:18:29,774
in front of that many people?

242
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:31,402
You must've had some plan.

243
00:18:33,237 --> 00:18:36,115
Don't try anything funny.

244
00:18:36,907 --> 00:18:39,200
If you do, I'll bring you in myself.

245
00:18:39,201 --> 00:18:42,288
You will always be the brother
of Baek Kitae.

246
00:18:43,456 --> 00:18:46,792
Jang Geonyoung is using you.
He'll chew you up and spit you out!

247
00:18:50,296 --> 00:18:52,006
Look, times have changed.

248
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:55,051
The KCIA is on its way out.

249
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:58,553
Chief Cheon's case is hopeless.
He's done for.

250
00:18:58,554 --> 00:19:01,307
But it's not too late for you
to walk away and go to Japan.

251
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:05,019
I'll be there for Soyeong and Minju.

252
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:09,815
You don't trust me anymore?
Is that what you're saying?

253
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:15,488
You've never been able to trust me.

254
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:08,581
Wow. It looks so great, Kihyun.

255
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:10,333
It screams "top of your class."

256
00:20:10,334 --> 00:20:12,836
He's top of his class,
do you hear that?

257
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:14,922
- Soyeong.
- Hmm?

258
00:20:16,340 --> 00:20:18,718
- I'm sorry.
- Sorry for what?

259
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:21,053
Just… all of it.

260
00:20:23,931 --> 00:20:27,268
Try to listen to Kitae.
I'll be all right. Hmm?

261
00:20:29,937 --> 00:20:31,354
Just wait a little longer.

262
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:32,897
As soon as I'm finished with school,

263
00:20:32,898 --> 00:20:34,899
I'll work hard
and give you the greatest life.

264
00:20:36,902 --> 00:20:38,237
- You mean it?
- Yeah.

265
00:20:39,113 --> 00:20:42,116
I'll always take care of you, don't worry.
I'll protect our family.

266
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:49,373
Come on, you're still just a kid.

267
00:20:50,541 --> 00:20:52,834
Take care of yourself
and eat plenty of food, you got that?

268
00:20:52,835 --> 00:20:53,836
Mm-hmm.

269
00:20:55,629 --> 00:20:58,132
-  Come on, you'll miss the train.
- Yes, sir.

270
00:21:01,969 --> 00:21:04,137
- Go inside. It's cold.
- All right, all right.

271
00:21:04,138 --> 00:21:06,766
- Go on.
- Yeah, I heard you.

272
00:21:09,769 --> 00:21:12,104
Write me, star cadet! Don't forget!

273
00:21:34,251 --> 00:21:35,252
You did well.

274
00:21:37,588 --> 00:21:39,089
Mom and Dad would be proud.

275
00:21:40,132 --> 00:21:41,675
And I don't say that lightly.

276
00:22:28,055 --> 00:22:30,015
What is it? Soyeong, you okay?

277
00:22:37,481 --> 00:22:38,482
Come on, here.

278
00:22:39,441 --> 00:22:40,442
It's okay.

279
00:22:41,193 --> 00:22:42,277
It's okay.

280
00:23:25,070 --> 00:23:26,363
When did you wake up?

281
00:23:28,782 --> 00:23:31,201
You better? You feeling all right?

282
00:23:45,215 --> 00:23:46,467
Why did you do it?

283
00:23:48,844 --> 00:23:51,221
Didn't I tell you
to stay away from that stuff?

284
00:23:53,557 --> 00:23:55,225
You been on it for a while?

285
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:58,520
Does Minju ever see you like this?

286
00:24:00,606 --> 00:24:03,108
Give me a break.
You made a fortune from meth.

287
00:24:04,276 --> 00:24:06,111
I'm sure you know a lot about us junkies.

288
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:20,834
Help me out.

289
00:24:23,337 --> 00:24:25,130
You can get me some, can't you?

290
00:24:26,674 --> 00:24:30,551
Just one last time. I swear.
I swear, all right? I swear.

291
00:24:30,552 --> 00:24:33,054
Gimme one more little bump.
Just one more time--

292
00:24:33,055 --> 00:24:35,265
-  Are you outta your mind?
- Stop it! Don't yell at me!

293
00:24:35,975 --> 00:24:39,728
Okay? You have no right
to raise your voice! Got it?

294
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:43,856
Minju's father is dead 'cause of you.

295
00:24:43,857 --> 00:24:47,026
You killed him, right? I heard everything.
You killed Daeil, didn't you?

296
00:24:49,238 --> 00:24:50,655
Who told you that?

297
00:24:58,122 --> 00:25:00,206
Poor Daeil…

298
00:25:00,207 --> 00:25:03,669
What did Daeil ever do
to deserve that? Huh?

299
00:25:05,254 --> 00:25:07,964
Everything you told us to do,

300
00:25:07,965 --> 00:25:10,718
we bent over backwards for it,
like idiots.

301
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:13,928
You son of a bitch.

302
00:25:13,929 --> 00:25:16,348
How could you do this to us?

303
00:25:17,808 --> 00:25:22,395
Do you know what it was like
for me to have Minju? Do you?

304
00:25:22,396 --> 00:25:25,399
Do you have any idea how hard it's been?

305
00:25:26,525 --> 00:25:29,861
Do you know what I've been through
all these years?

306
00:25:34,116 --> 00:25:37,201
Oh, Daeil, that poor man.

307
00:25:52,634 --> 00:25:54,178
Don't worry about anything.

308
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:58,098
Minju still needs you.

309
00:25:59,391 --> 00:26:01,101
Try to accept the treatment…

310
00:26:03,645 --> 00:26:05,397
then you'll be on your feet soon.

311
00:26:06,273 --> 00:26:07,858
Don't come back here.

312
00:26:08,358 --> 00:26:10,610
Soyeong.

313
00:26:10,611 --> 00:26:13,030
Just pretend I'm dead.

314
00:26:13,906 --> 00:26:15,949
Don't you ever come see me again!

315
00:26:17,201 --> 00:26:18,202
I'm such…

316
00:26:19,328 --> 00:26:20,953
such an idiot.

317
00:26:20,954 --> 00:26:23,706
I'm such an idiot!

318
00:26:23,707 --> 00:26:27,794
I can't face her like this!
How will I ever look at Minju again?

319
00:27:00,077 --> 00:27:03,747
Commander, we appreciate
you having us over to your home, sir.

320
00:27:04,623 --> 00:27:07,167
I mean, it's subpar, I'd say.

321
00:27:08,168 --> 00:27:11,337
I was never good
at putting money aside, honestly.

322
00:27:11,338 --> 00:27:13,381
I wouldn't have been able
to afford this house

323
00:27:13,382 --> 00:27:15,258
if my wife hadn't budgeted so well.

324
00:27:15,259 --> 00:27:17,553
-  How 'bout that.
- It's the truth.

325
00:27:18,637 --> 00:27:19,804
Colonel Baek.

326
00:27:19,805 --> 00:27:21,556
The house may not look too great,

327
00:27:21,557 --> 00:27:24,350
but I'm gonna make sure
you eat as much as you want.

328
00:27:24,351 --> 00:27:25,894
Yes, sir. Much appreciated.

329
00:27:26,645 --> 00:27:28,856
Here, how about a drink?

330
00:27:36,697 --> 00:27:38,573
You've been working hard

331
00:27:38,574 --> 00:27:41,869
to dig up more information
on Chief Cheon's slush fund, I take it.

332
00:27:43,245 --> 00:27:45,831
Since you trusted me with it,
I have to give it my all.

333
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:47,666
He's the best man for it.

334
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:52,670
I know it involves your family.
That's difficult.

335
00:27:52,671 --> 00:27:55,841
Still, Baek, I'm willing to bet
you're the man for this investigation.

336
00:27:56,633 --> 00:27:57,885
I'll do my very best.

337
00:27:58,677 --> 00:28:00,261
Great! We are…

338
00:28:00,262 --> 00:28:01,346
- One.
- One.

339
00:28:05,267 --> 00:28:06,894
Ah, geez.

340
00:28:08,395 --> 00:28:12,481
If we're gonna have special guests over,
we should be serving something special.

341
00:28:12,482 --> 00:28:14,275
My wife never listens.

342
00:28:14,276 --> 00:28:15,985
Let's see.

343
00:28:15,986 --> 00:28:18,571
Okay, here we go.

344
00:28:18,572 --> 00:28:20,448
Hey, Colonel Ahn, grab this kettle here.

345
00:28:20,449 --> 00:28:21,450
Yes, sir, I'm on it.

346
00:28:22,576 --> 00:28:24,744
All right, Kihyun.

347
00:28:24,745 --> 00:28:26,914
Check out this piece of work. Eh?

348
00:28:28,248 --> 00:28:30,876
A guy a couple years below me
at the Academy sent it over.

349
00:28:34,046 --> 00:28:37,381
He got injured during training,
and then, he had to resign.

350
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:39,634
And now he's out
in the middle of nowhere growing ginseng.

351
00:28:39,635 --> 00:28:42,094
Chungsik, sir? He was my classmate.

352
00:28:42,095 --> 00:28:44,639
That's right.
You were in the same year, weren't you?

353
00:28:44,640 --> 00:28:46,182
Yes, we were.

354
00:28:46,183 --> 00:28:49,311
This here?
Chungsik actually made this himself.

355
00:28:49,895 --> 00:28:52,648
Are you sure you want to share
something so valuable, sir?

356
00:28:53,231 --> 00:28:56,901
The man sends me a new one
every single year.

357
00:28:59,863 --> 00:29:01,614
He's got three kids,

358
00:29:01,615 --> 00:29:03,574
and I put all three through college.

359
00:29:03,575 --> 00:29:05,076
I was happy to do it.

360
00:29:05,077 --> 00:29:07,996
So that pot of honey,
was that from an officer as well?

361
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:09,664
Sure was.

362
00:29:09,665 --> 00:29:12,375
That stuff is priceless,
can't get it anywhere.

363
00:29:12,376 --> 00:29:15,462
And at the end of the day,
it's the thought that counts.

364
00:29:16,088 --> 00:29:17,421
You're right, sir.

365
00:29:17,422 --> 00:29:20,592
You have something of a reputation
for looking after young officers.

366
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:24,429
How do you manage to support
and take care of so many?

367
00:29:28,809 --> 00:29:29,810
I have a question.

368
00:29:31,228 --> 00:29:33,230
What do you think it means
to be a soldier?

369
00:29:34,022 --> 00:29:36,691
To be loyal to the country
and to be devoted to its defense.

370
00:29:36,692 --> 00:29:38,150
Correct.

371
00:29:38,151 --> 00:29:40,237
Loyalty and devotion.

372
00:29:41,446 --> 00:29:43,948
A soldier puts his mortal life
on the line.

373
00:29:43,949 --> 00:29:45,157
And how do you think it feels

374
00:29:45,158 --> 00:29:47,577
when your country
doesn't recognize that? Huh?

375
00:29:48,578 --> 00:29:51,957
Every soldier needs someone
that acknowledges their sacrifice.

376
00:29:53,375 --> 00:29:55,669
To that end…

377
00:30:00,716 --> 00:30:03,093
if you say you've got my back…

378
00:30:05,178 --> 00:30:08,889
then I will have yours to the bitter end.

379
00:30:10,934 --> 00:30:12,185
You understand?

380
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:16,772
And your family is included, too.

381
00:30:23,864 --> 00:30:25,699
One scoop of creamer…

382
00:30:26,742 --> 00:30:28,326
and one scoop of sugar.

383
00:30:30,412 --> 00:30:31,455
That's it.

384
00:30:32,497 --> 00:30:34,207
I've tried it a few different ways,

385
00:30:35,250 --> 00:30:37,376
and I've discovered
this is the perfect balance…

386
00:30:37,377 --> 00:30:39,379
…for this brew.

387
00:30:41,006 --> 00:30:42,215
Okay. Here you go.

388
00:30:47,929 --> 00:30:50,265
Ah.

389
00:30:51,266 --> 00:30:53,602
Ah, that's nice.

390
00:30:56,688 --> 00:30:59,316
All the assemblymen
who used to treat you like royalty…

391
00:31:00,150 --> 00:31:01,567
I've talked to them, you know?

392
00:31:01,568 --> 00:31:03,778
I interrogated them one by one.

393
00:31:03,779 --> 00:31:04,904
Understand?

394
00:31:04,905 --> 00:31:09,158
They're the kind of people that love
clinging to power when they can,

395
00:31:09,159 --> 00:31:13,204
but suddenly, the moment it's gone,
they all scatter like roaches.

396
00:31:13,205 --> 00:31:14,914
Classic opportunists.

397
00:31:14,915 --> 00:31:16,582
We both know that power comes and goes.

398
00:31:16,583 --> 00:31:18,418
It can be elusive as the wind.

399
00:31:19,086 --> 00:31:22,421
Even the mighty Korean oak
sheds its leaves eventually.

400
00:31:22,422 --> 00:31:24,925
Hwang Daesik won't be around forever.

401
00:31:30,555 --> 00:31:32,808
So you like… oak trees?

402
00:31:34,726 --> 00:31:38,647
Careful, one wrong move with me,
you'll get chopped up for kindling.

403
00:31:39,981 --> 00:31:41,607
Hmm?

404
00:31:41,608 --> 00:31:43,400
All right,
why don't you throw in the towel

405
00:31:43,401 --> 00:31:45,319
while you still have some dignity?

406
00:31:45,320 --> 00:31:47,863
Come on, you were a guy with influence,

407
00:31:47,864 --> 00:31:50,492
standing right next
to the most important men in Korea.

408
00:31:51,118 --> 00:31:54,121
Want to spend the rest of your life
rotting on the forest floor?

409
00:31:54,830 --> 00:31:57,082
Have some self-respect. You're through.

410
00:31:58,125 --> 00:31:59,750
Turn Baek Kitae in and confess.

411
00:32:11,054 --> 00:32:14,015
You shoved my head
into the crapper, Mister Jang.

412
00:32:17,227 --> 00:32:19,146
My self-respect is long gone.

413
00:32:36,788 --> 00:32:39,040
I wonder
what you're hoping for.

414
00:32:39,624 --> 00:32:41,626
Why bide your time, Chief Cheon?

415
00:32:43,420 --> 00:32:45,881
I know there's a reason
you're holding out.

416
00:32:48,592 --> 00:32:51,136
Know what, why don't I just take a guess?

417
00:33:15,869 --> 00:33:17,453
I think you're waiting.

418
00:33:20,540 --> 00:33:21,791
You're waiting for…

419
00:33:25,295 --> 00:33:26,922
Hwang Daesik to die.

420
00:33:35,513 --> 00:33:36,640
Busted.

421
00:33:53,198 --> 00:33:55,115
Pyo Haksu just compiled these dossiers.

422
00:33:55,116 --> 00:33:56,867
They're all members of the JIH.

423
00:33:56,868 --> 00:33:58,118
OFFICER PERSONNEL RECORD

424
00:33:58,119 --> 00:34:01,247
Why don't you take a look
for potential new informants?

425
00:34:01,248 --> 00:34:02,540
Yes, Director Baek.

426
00:34:05,418 --> 00:34:06,419
Sir, I've been wondering…

427
00:34:07,629 --> 00:34:09,256
what did Colonel Baek say?

428
00:34:11,341 --> 00:34:12,634
Did he put it together?

429
00:34:13,218 --> 00:34:14,511
Don't worry about that.

430
00:34:15,428 --> 00:34:16,638
I'll take care of it.

431
00:34:19,057 --> 00:34:21,934
Why do you think he didn't tell us
he was going to be there?

432
00:34:21,935 --> 00:34:23,478
I don't understand, sir. If…

433
00:34:24,229 --> 00:34:27,065
if our strategy was exposed beforehand,
wouldn't that mean…

434
00:34:31,945 --> 00:34:33,113
I apologize.

435
00:34:39,286 --> 00:34:41,538
- Kihun…
- Yes, Director?

436
00:34:43,581 --> 00:34:44,708
We need…

437
00:34:45,583 --> 00:34:47,334
more explosives, right away.

438
00:34:47,335 --> 00:34:48,544
Huh?

439
00:34:51,047 --> 00:34:52,131
We do?

440
00:34:52,132 --> 00:34:54,676
You start something,
you have to finish it.

441
00:34:56,803 --> 00:35:00,014
With all due respect,
we lost the last batch, sir.

442
00:35:00,015 --> 00:35:02,016
Someone's already aware of this.

443
00:35:02,017 --> 00:35:04,144
And that means
we have to hurry and finish it.

444
00:35:06,187 --> 00:35:07,314
That's how…

445
00:35:08,940 --> 00:35:10,191
we survive this.

446
00:35:36,676 --> 00:35:37,844
Colonel Baek.

447
00:35:38,928 --> 00:35:41,972
You had dinner last night,
at General Hwang's house.

448
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:44,225
- Is that true?
- Yes.

449
00:35:45,852 --> 00:35:47,020
Okay. Well?

450
00:35:48,938 --> 00:35:50,315
Have you made a decision?

451
00:35:51,775 --> 00:35:53,652
Made a decision about what, sir?

452
00:35:56,946 --> 00:35:57,989
Hold on.

453
00:35:59,741 --> 00:36:02,410
You're still making up your mind? Really?

454
00:36:03,203 --> 00:36:06,915
You playing Hamlet or something? Huh?

455
00:36:17,926 --> 00:36:19,260
Sit down for a second.

456
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:37,654
Right, I'll be direct with you.

457
00:36:39,072 --> 00:36:40,573
Let's talk about your brother.

458
00:36:43,576 --> 00:36:46,454
I want to know why he showed up
at Heaven Cloud Pavilion.

459
00:36:48,540 --> 00:36:49,791
You know, don't you?

460
00:36:51,042 --> 00:36:52,836
He showed up, out of nowhere.

461
00:36:54,295 --> 00:36:55,505
Can you tell me why?

462
00:36:58,758 --> 00:37:00,885
You're thinking the same thing I am,
aren't you?

463
00:37:04,055 --> 00:37:06,306
I think we have the exact same theory.

464
00:37:10,311 --> 00:37:11,521
Baek Kitae…

465
00:37:13,231 --> 00:37:14,607
was trying to take out…

466
00:37:15,692 --> 00:37:16,985
General Hwang Daesik.

467
00:37:18,319 --> 00:37:19,945
But then,

468
00:37:19,946 --> 00:37:21,948
all of a sudden,
his little brother showed up.

469
00:37:23,450 --> 00:37:24,951
You threw a wrench into it.

470
00:37:30,790 --> 00:37:32,459
Do you have any proof?

471
00:37:34,502 --> 00:37:35,962
That he did any of that?

472
00:37:38,840 --> 00:37:40,258
If I had solid proof…

473
00:37:44,721 --> 00:37:46,931
you think I'd be dumb enough
to let him walk?

474
00:37:49,267 --> 00:37:52,394
Don't go around accusing people
without any proof.

475
00:37:52,395 --> 00:37:55,231
I'm only saying this
out of the goodness of my heart.

476
00:37:56,566 --> 00:37:59,318
The entire KCIA has
already been credibly accused

477
00:37:59,319 --> 00:38:02,071
of conspiring to assassinate
the President, Colonel.

478
00:38:04,783 --> 00:38:05,950
If Baek Kitae tries…

479
00:38:07,285 --> 00:38:09,829
to kill General Hwang,
you know what that means,

480
00:38:10,538 --> 00:38:11,539
don't you?

481
00:38:12,624 --> 00:38:16,753
You and your entire family… are done.

482
00:38:20,089 --> 00:38:21,841
Oh, that will never happen.

483
00:38:23,843 --> 00:38:25,011
It better not.

484
00:38:30,308 --> 00:38:32,059
-  Sorry to interrupt, sir.
- Mmm.

485
00:38:32,060 --> 00:38:34,229
Director Baek suddenly showed up.

486
00:38:36,689 --> 00:38:38,482
Wants to see his brother, huh?

487
00:38:38,483 --> 00:38:41,820
Actually… he says
he wants to speak with you.

488
00:38:46,032 --> 00:38:49,952
Ah, so he's here to have a chat with me,
not Colonel Baek, huh?

489
00:38:49,953 --> 00:38:51,036
Yes, sir.

490
00:39:07,846 --> 00:39:09,430
Director Baek, good to see you.

491
00:39:11,683 --> 00:39:12,767
I'll show you inside.

492
00:39:15,979 --> 00:39:17,146
Afternoon, sir!

493
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:27,365
This way, sir.

494
00:39:37,709 --> 00:39:39,293
- Captain Min.
- Yes, sir.

495
00:39:39,294 --> 00:39:42,297
JOINT INVESTIGATION HEADQUARTERS
INVESTIGATION DIVISION

496
00:39:44,382 --> 00:39:45,633
Shall we step inside?

497
00:39:55,435 --> 00:39:56,686
This way, please.

498
00:40:19,626 --> 00:40:21,209
Well, hello, Prosecutor.

499
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:24,255
Can I… help you, Director Baek?

500
00:40:30,345 --> 00:40:31,929
Watch yourself if you wanna live.

501
00:40:47,695 --> 00:40:50,030
- Yes?
- It's Colonel Ahn Jaeho, sir.

502
00:40:50,031 --> 00:40:51,199
Come in.

503
00:41:04,629 --> 00:41:05,880
All right, Colonel.

504
00:41:06,506 --> 00:41:08,049
Give us a little privacy.

505
00:41:09,342 --> 00:41:10,510
Yes, of course.

506
00:41:30,697 --> 00:41:32,031
What brings you here?

507
00:41:33,658 --> 00:41:36,911
Well, I heard they gathered
the finest operatives in Korea…

508
00:41:38,037 --> 00:41:40,456
so I thought I'd come by
and take a look around.

509
00:41:41,791 --> 00:41:43,251
And? What do you think?

510
00:41:43,918 --> 00:41:46,421
They're all here to bring down
an evil prick like you.

511
00:41:47,505 --> 00:41:48,923
All this for me, huh?

512
00:41:50,883 --> 00:41:53,468
Hwang Daesik really
put this operation together

513
00:41:53,469 --> 00:41:55,263
just to catch one lousy guy?

514
00:42:01,853 --> 00:42:03,604
Why are you here, Baek?

515
00:42:10,194 --> 00:42:12,989
Leave Kihyun alone.
I'd really appreciate it.

516
00:42:13,906 --> 00:42:15,991
That's pretty polite for a threat.

517
00:42:15,992 --> 00:42:18,618
If you screw with my family,
I'll hurt yours.

518
00:42:18,619 --> 00:42:20,079
You piece of shit.

519
00:42:21,914 --> 00:42:25,292
Wow, you'll hurt anybody as long
as it's not your own flesh and blood.

520
00:42:25,293 --> 00:42:26,878
If you're afraid for them, then stop this.

521
00:42:28,296 --> 00:42:30,173
That's how you protect your loved ones.

522
00:42:31,132 --> 00:42:32,216
Put an end to it.

523
00:42:38,306 --> 00:42:40,683
Do you really think
I can stop at this point?

524
00:42:58,534 --> 00:43:00,244
There was this officer once.

525
00:43:01,537 --> 00:43:04,707
This was back in the army.
And, whew, this bastard gave me hell.

526
00:43:05,333 --> 00:43:09,087
He was always smacking me around,
cursing me out.

527
00:43:10,338 --> 00:43:12,840
I must have made
a good punching bag for him,

528
00:43:13,716 --> 00:43:15,218
'cause my family had no connections.

529
00:43:16,427 --> 00:43:19,638
So I wondered what kind of rich,
privileged household

530
00:43:19,639 --> 00:43:22,391
this asshole came from
that entitled him to act like that.

531
00:43:23,226 --> 00:43:26,938
Turns out this guy
had no connections either.

532
00:43:27,522 --> 00:43:30,732
He was raised in a dirt-poor family.
They had nothing.

533
00:43:30,733 --> 00:43:32,443
People looked down on them constantly.

534
00:43:33,986 --> 00:43:36,404
And this poor bastard
was picked on like crazy.

535
00:43:38,866 --> 00:43:41,284
That's why he couldn't resist

536
00:43:41,285 --> 00:43:44,330
making life hard
for people who were just like him.

537
00:43:45,790 --> 00:43:48,584
Two losers who were born with jack shit,

538
00:43:49,252 --> 00:43:51,295
ripping each other apart
for the hell of it.

539
00:43:55,258 --> 00:43:56,425
Know what I thought…

540
00:43:57,468 --> 00:44:00,263
when that son of a bitch would
start beating the shit out of me?

541
00:44:00,972 --> 00:44:03,599
"First I'll kill this asshole,
then I'll kill myself"?

542
00:44:04,100 --> 00:44:05,101
That's right.

543
00:44:06,894 --> 00:44:08,813
"This sick bastard is going down.

544
00:44:09,981 --> 00:44:11,315
Then I'll follow."

545
00:44:15,403 --> 00:44:17,280
You know exactly what that feels like.

546
00:44:20,074 --> 00:44:21,200
Baek Kitae.

547
00:44:22,785 --> 00:44:24,412
I already lived through that once.

548
00:44:25,204 --> 00:44:27,039
You think I'm going
to let it happen again?

549
00:44:28,040 --> 00:44:30,542
If you don't pump the brakes
and stop what you're doing,

550
00:44:30,543 --> 00:44:31,752
neither will I.

551
00:44:33,671 --> 00:44:35,798
This only ends when one of us is dead.

552
00:44:37,258 --> 00:44:39,677
Wow, that's dramatic.

553
00:44:41,554 --> 00:44:42,889
I hear you.

554
00:44:44,932 --> 00:44:46,809
Now let me ask you a favor, Mr. Jang.

555
00:44:48,019 --> 00:44:49,937
Let me see Chief Cheon immediately.

556
00:44:52,148 --> 00:44:54,317
His whole family's been very worried.

557
00:44:55,318 --> 00:44:57,278
I mean, he's not even allowed visitors.

558
00:44:57,778 --> 00:45:01,032
His wife came to see me the other day
and begged me to try to help.

559
00:45:02,325 --> 00:45:03,576
Can you make that happen?

560
00:45:05,786 --> 00:45:07,121
Just a brief chat.

561
00:45:27,725 --> 00:45:29,143
We found Park Changbae.

562
00:45:37,485 --> 00:45:39,110
…SCENE INVESTIGATION REPORT
ON BODY FOUND

563
00:45:39,111 --> 00:45:41,196
His body was dumped
up in the hills.

564
00:45:41,197 --> 00:45:42,406
It's Baek Kitae.

565
00:45:44,075 --> 00:45:45,284
He made this happen.

566
00:45:45,993 --> 00:45:49,622
He's on a mission to wipe out
every last trace of his drug operation.

567
00:45:51,082 --> 00:45:52,750
But what's his angle right now?

568
00:45:54,043 --> 00:45:56,671
He had to have come into the office
for a reason.

569
00:46:21,070 --> 00:46:22,655
So how are you holding up, sir?

570
00:46:23,489 --> 00:46:24,782
I'm all right.

571
00:46:25,741 --> 00:46:27,285
And how about you?

572
00:46:29,537 --> 00:46:31,080
You look like a million bucks.

573
00:46:35,376 --> 00:46:37,544
Your wife is upset.
She's worried about you.

574
00:46:37,545 --> 00:46:38,963
Why is she worried?

575
00:46:40,589 --> 00:46:43,509
I'm still eating and shitting.
Tell my wife to relax.

576
00:46:45,136 --> 00:46:47,638
And remind her to walk Gaettong
when she can.

577
00:46:49,390 --> 00:46:51,600
If that little mutt
doesn't get his exercise…

578
00:46:52,643 --> 00:46:54,020
he gets ferocious.

579
00:46:55,563 --> 00:46:56,772
Yes, I'll remind her.

580
00:46:57,857 --> 00:47:00,651
Are there any other messages
you want me to pass along?

581
00:47:02,320 --> 00:47:04,864
Lend me a smoke.

582
00:47:22,923 --> 00:47:24,550
There's one other thing.

583
00:47:25,343 --> 00:47:28,470
My father's memorial is coming up, but I…

584
00:47:28,471 --> 00:47:30,765
haven't cleaned up his grave
since Chuseok.

585
00:47:32,141 --> 00:47:34,184
Don't worry, I'll take care of it.

586
00:47:34,185 --> 00:47:35,519
Really?

587
00:47:36,979 --> 00:47:39,065
I'd appreciate that very much.

588
00:47:44,570 --> 00:47:46,113
When you gonna do it?

589
00:47:48,366 --> 00:47:50,658
The grass must be
pretty overgrown by now.

590
00:47:50,659 --> 00:47:53,329
If you're going to take care of it,
you should get it done soon.

591
00:47:54,622 --> 00:47:57,124
I'm on it, sir. I'll do it this week.

592
00:47:59,293 --> 00:48:00,878
Okay, that's perfect.

593
00:48:03,714 --> 00:48:06,258
The weeds are gonna
be pretty tough at this point.

594
00:48:08,761 --> 00:48:10,429
Just pull them all out.

595
00:48:13,724 --> 00:48:14,809
Yes, sir. I will.

596
00:48:18,145 --> 00:48:19,980
Doesn't that sound a little suspicious?

597
00:48:21,232 --> 00:48:22,233
What does?

598
00:48:23,109 --> 00:48:24,193
I mean…

599
00:48:25,361 --> 00:48:26,569
Well, I don't know.

600
00:48:26,570 --> 00:48:28,114
The way they're talking.

601
00:48:28,739 --> 00:48:30,783
What's suspicious about it?

602
00:48:33,327 --> 00:48:34,495
Baek Kitae…

603
00:48:35,830 --> 00:48:38,749
is just offering to help clean up
his father's grave site.

604
00:48:44,588 --> 00:48:47,298
People do each other favors
like that all the time.

605
00:49:32,136 --> 00:49:33,761
Did you see him, sir?

606
00:49:33,762 --> 00:49:34,847
Uh-huh.

607
00:49:36,599 --> 00:49:38,392
Do you think that Jang suspects anything?

608
00:49:45,900 --> 00:49:47,109
Um, sir?

609
00:49:48,444 --> 00:49:49,612
What do we do?

610
00:49:52,823 --> 00:49:53,948
Continue as planned.

611
00:50:11,675 --> 00:50:13,511
- Are you sure?
-  Yes, sir.

612
00:50:14,094 --> 00:50:16,722
I have a buddy in Foreign Intelligence.
He told me himself.

613
00:50:17,389 --> 00:50:19,225
An order came through not long ago.

614
00:50:19,934 --> 00:50:22,101
They must've had trouble
getting a new round of explosives.

615
00:50:22,102 --> 00:50:23,771
- Hey.
- Yes, sir?

616
00:50:24,313 --> 00:50:26,607
- What's with the sniffling?
- Sorry, sir.

617
00:50:27,358 --> 00:50:28,691
Sinus infection.

618
00:50:28,692 --> 00:50:30,109
- You.
- Yes, sir?

619
00:50:30,110 --> 00:50:31,736
Find out what they're for.

620
00:50:31,737 --> 00:50:35,199
When, where,
and how they're gonna use those.

621
00:50:36,617 --> 00:50:37,618
I'll take care of it.

622
00:50:39,161 --> 00:50:40,287
Find out for sure.

623
00:50:41,080 --> 00:50:42,164
- Yes, sir.
- Go.

624
00:50:49,755 --> 00:50:51,382
Baek Kitae, that bastard.

625
00:50:53,133 --> 00:50:54,426
Sly little shit.

626
00:51:19,368 --> 00:51:20,536
Captain Min Jonghwan.

627
00:51:21,745 --> 00:51:22,746
You know who I am?

628
00:51:24,498 --> 00:51:25,499
Yes.

629
00:51:27,334 --> 00:51:28,377
I, uh…

630
00:51:33,757 --> 00:51:35,050
Where am I, sir?

631
00:51:37,678 --> 00:51:38,971
And what am I doing here?

632
00:51:40,889 --> 00:51:43,267
You telling me you really don't know?

633
00:51:43,851 --> 00:51:45,019
No, I'm sorry, sir.

634
00:51:45,894 --> 00:51:48,104
I really have no idea
what you're talking about. I mean it.

635
00:51:50,357 --> 00:51:52,693
- Gonna act clueless, huh?
- No, sir.

636
00:51:54,153 --> 00:51:56,280
Did I screw up or something?
What happened?

637
00:51:58,073 --> 00:52:00,241
PERSONAL RECORD OF DEFECTOR
TO NORTH KOREA - PARK JEONGPIL

638
00:52:00,242 --> 00:52:02,703
Says here your uncle
defected to the North.

639
00:52:04,079 --> 00:52:05,663
Are you a spy?

640
00:52:05,664 --> 00:52:09,001
A commie in Military Security Command?
What's your angle?

641
00:52:16,800 --> 00:52:17,801
Come on!

642
00:52:20,512 --> 00:52:21,804
Are you a spy?

643
00:52:21,805 --> 00:52:22,890
No, I'm not.

644
00:52:25,517 --> 00:52:26,518
So…

645
00:52:32,983 --> 00:52:34,400
Could I bum a smoke from you, sir?

646
00:52:34,401 --> 00:52:35,694
You little shit…

647
00:53:05,391 --> 00:53:08,227
I cut ties with that side
of the family a long time ago.

648
00:53:10,896 --> 00:53:12,356
As for my uncle…

649
00:53:14,316 --> 00:53:16,485
I joined MSC before I learned about it.

650
00:53:17,194 --> 00:53:18,821
How did you even get in?

651
00:53:21,907 --> 00:53:23,951
The officer who hired me, uh…

652
00:53:25,953 --> 00:53:27,495
expunged my file.

653
00:53:27,496 --> 00:53:29,373
He erased your record, huh?

654
00:53:30,374 --> 00:53:31,375
Why?

655
00:53:33,877 --> 00:53:36,505
I did him one favor.
And it was pretty difficult.

656
00:53:41,510 --> 00:53:43,303
And in return, he fixed my record.

657
00:53:51,603 --> 00:53:54,398
You're the KCIA director.
You're a powerful man, right?

658
00:53:55,816 --> 00:53:57,818
You probably wouldn't
go through the trouble

659
00:53:58,485 --> 00:54:00,654
to screw over a low-level captain.

660
00:54:02,740 --> 00:54:04,116
What is it you want from me, sir?

661
00:54:05,826 --> 00:54:07,327
Your mind works fast.

662
00:54:11,707 --> 00:54:14,167
And there's ambition in your eyes.
That's good.

663
00:54:31,518 --> 00:54:32,811
There we go.

664
00:54:34,480 --> 00:54:37,065
KOREAN CENTRAL
INTELLIGENCE AGENCY

665
00:54:48,327 --> 00:54:49,328
"Min Jong…"

666
00:54:52,539 --> 00:54:54,415
It's confirmed.
Colonel Baek won't be attending

667
00:54:54,416 --> 00:54:56,167
the Joint Investigation
Headquarters meeting.

668
00:54:56,168 --> 00:54:58,377
HWANG DAESIK, JO HYEONGU, AHN
JAEHO… MIN JONGHWAN, KIM DONGMIN

669
00:54:58,378 --> 00:55:00,756
He'll be at a Martial Law Command meeting
at Army Headquarters instead.

670
00:55:05,177 --> 00:55:06,385
He'll be gone, sir.

671
00:55:06,386 --> 00:55:09,389
He'll leave the building a full 30 minutes
ahead of the operation.

672
00:55:10,057 --> 00:55:11,225
So don't worry about him.

673
00:55:33,247 --> 00:55:36,667
They're all getting together for a meeting
tomorrow at the JIH, 10:00 a.m.

674
00:55:37,709 --> 00:55:39,169
All you have to do is…

675
00:55:40,128 --> 00:55:42,547
get the briefcase in there
before the meeting starts.

676
00:55:42,548 --> 00:55:44,675
You know I'll be the first one
they suspect.

677
00:55:45,842 --> 00:55:47,135
And even if it works,

678
00:55:48,053 --> 00:55:49,721
I'm as good as dead, aren't I?

679
00:55:50,847 --> 00:55:52,808
If you don't do it,
you'll die here.

680
00:55:53,559 --> 00:55:54,935
But if you succeed,

681
00:55:56,228 --> 00:55:58,313
you might actually survive in the end.

682
00:56:04,152 --> 00:56:05,571
I'll help you.

683
00:56:07,322 --> 00:56:08,740
If it ends up working…

684
00:56:10,784 --> 00:56:12,494
you better help me out.

685
00:56:14,788 --> 00:56:16,957
What, you want me to make you a general?

686
00:56:17,791 --> 00:56:19,668
You can kill yourself being loyal,

687
00:56:20,961 --> 00:56:22,379
but without power…

688
00:56:24,756 --> 00:56:26,300
you'll always be invisible.

689
00:56:33,557 --> 00:56:35,183
I have to take this gamble.

690
00:57:25,734 --> 00:57:27,110
You know who this is?

691
00:57:29,029 --> 00:57:30,489
Min Jonghwan, really?

692
00:57:31,490 --> 00:57:33,158
It was him?

693
00:57:33,659 --> 00:57:35,661
There's something else
you should probably know.

694
00:57:40,123 --> 00:57:42,125
Baek got explosives recently.

695
00:57:44,878 --> 00:57:47,046
Word is, he's bought some before.

696
00:57:49,675 --> 00:57:51,510
Do you know anything about that?

697
00:57:54,513 --> 00:57:56,056
Well, it looks like you do.

698
00:57:58,392 --> 00:57:59,559
Hmm…

699
00:58:00,560 --> 00:58:02,688
And he's got agents standing by tomorrow.

700
00:58:04,314 --> 00:58:05,856
Really?

701
00:58:05,857 --> 00:58:06,858
You see?

702
00:58:09,736 --> 00:58:11,488
It's all coming together.

703
00:58:12,656 --> 00:58:15,409
There's a regular meeting
at the JIH tomorrow, right?

704
00:58:16,952 --> 00:58:18,829
Hwang Daesik will be there for sure.

705
00:58:21,206 --> 00:58:22,624
Gonna be interesting.

706
00:58:28,255 --> 00:58:30,757
So… what's the plan, then?

707
00:58:45,147 --> 00:58:46,606
You better do this right.

708
01:01:29,519 --> 01:01:32,730
♪ Through
Lofty mountains and deep valleys ♪

709
01:01:32,731 --> 01:01:37,067
♪ Across the silent land ♪

710
01:01:37,068 --> 01:01:43,365
♪ We march to the snow-covered frontline ♪

711
01:01:43,366 --> 01:01:44,700
The ground!

712
01:01:44,701 --> 01:01:48,621
♪ The ground where young souls ♪

713
01:01:48,622 --> 01:01:51,957
♪ Fell and perished ♪

714
01:01:51,958 --> 01:01:53,042
The wounded!

715
01:01:53,043 --> 01:01:56,503
♪ The wounded!
Old pines have fallen silent ♪

716
01:01:56,504 --> 01:01:58,005
Oh, what the hell!

717
01:01:58,006 --> 01:02:00,215
-  ♪ Have fallen silent ♪
-  Comrade!

718
01:02:00,216 --> 01:02:02,676
♪ Comrade, can you hear… ♪

719
01:02:02,677 --> 01:02:04,887
What are you doing?
Get out of there.

720
01:02:04,888 --> 01:02:07,014
Stop it. Look what he's doing.

721
01:02:07,015 --> 01:02:09,350
Someone's had a little too much to drink.

722
01:02:09,351 --> 01:02:11,393
What are you looking for under there?

723
01:02:11,394 --> 01:02:13,938
You're embarrassing me, you dirty old man.

724
01:02:13,939 --> 01:02:16,148
♪ Those eyes
Filled with bitter grief? ♪

725
01:02:19,235 --> 01:02:21,738
We are one!
